From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Tue, 11 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: Reclaim the variable store before the option
 lock

SMMSTORE_OPTION_LOCK, armed at ReadyToBoot, refuses a write of the fault
tolerant write blocks once armed (the restart of a pending one would let
the store be rewritten with a protected option off). A reclaim of the
variable store uses those blocks, so it must run before the lock is
armed. PcdReclaimVariableSpaceAtEndOfDxe moves the reclaim from
ReadyToBoot to EndOfDxe, which is before it; a runtime reclaim, when the
store is full, is refused and the variable write fails until the next
boot, which reclaims again.

---
 UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dsc | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dsc b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dsc
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dsc
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dsc
@@ -811,6 +811,7 @@
   gEfiMdeModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdMaxVariableSize|0x8000
   gEfiMdeModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdMaxHardwareErrorVariableSize|0x8000
   gEfiMdeModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdVariableStoreSize|0x10000
+  gEfiMdeModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdReclaimVariableSpaceAtEndOfDxe|TRUE
 !if $(VARIABLE_SUPPORT) == "EMU"
   gEfiMdeModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdEmuVariableNvModeEnable        |TRUE
 !elseif $(VARIABLE_SUPPORT) == "SPI" || $(VARIABLE_SUPPORT) == "SMMSTORE"
-- 
